Qualitative Classification
In qualitative classification, data is classified on the
basis of descriptive characteristics or on the basis of
attributes like sex literacy, region, caste, education,
etc. which cannot be quantified.
Simple Classification: When facts are classified into
two classes according to one attribute only, then the
classification is said to be simple.
